{"id":"20260830T003210.374609309Z-07a9486a","time":"2026-08-30T00:32:10.374609309Z","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeXzS9V5ibARvCrPC9vkc\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1699,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":158858,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1699},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"387957e3-29eb-4042-bbfa-afa88be0c2c6\",\"uuid\":\"448eebf2-3280-4910-a3f5-ad99c1ddec7b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-30T00:32:10.372Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeXzS8WnjaUFQpPAkoBdJ\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260830T003232.575106673Z-09f8aea7","time":"2026-08-30T00:32:32.575106673Z","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeXzS9V5ibARvCrPC9vkc\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All checks pass. Here's what I did.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**1. `internal/gitx/git.go` — authoritative changed paths**\\nAdded `Status`, `FileChange`, `ChangeSet`, `(Repo).ChangeSet`, `parseNameStatusZ`, `nameStatus`. `ChangeSet` runs `git diff --no-ext-diff --name-status -z \u003cbase\u003e --` (same arg shape as `CandidateCapture`, so both describe the same candidate) and parses on NUL boundaries — nothing split on whitespace, nothing trimmed. Both sides of a rename are kept; `Paths()` returns both, because a rename removes a path as surely as a deletion. Sorted after parsing.\\n\\n**2. `internal/report/report.go` — quoted headers**\\n`diffPath` now reads a `diff --git \\\"a/…\\\" \\\"b/…\\\"` header, `rename from`/`rename to` unquote, and the `+++` fallback goes through `sidePath` (declines `/dev/null`). Added `scanQuoted`/`unquoteC`, which undo Git's C escapes **byte-wise** — octal escapes are reassembled as bytes, so a pathname that isn't valid UTF-8 survives. Malformed quoting is refused, not half-read. Still a renderer.\\n\\n**3. `internal/workflow/testedit.go` — `confineToPlan(changed, planned)`**\\nCompares exactly as Git reports: no `TrimSpace` on either side, no case folding, no separator rewriting. The plan's side is canonicalised by `path.Clean` only (which never touches whitespace, so it can't fold two distinct paths into one). Takes no grant.\\n\\n**4. `internal/workflow/engine.go`**\\n- `confineCandidate` + `reconcileChangeSet`: obtains the ChangeSet, reconciles paths/statuses/rename-old-paths against `report.FromDiff`, refuses naming the disagreement, then confines.\\n- Called at **both** binding points — immediately after the `ModeInspect` refusal, and immediately after `e.validate` returns (so a formatter that widens the candidate during validation is caught).\\n- Terminal completion: after the review resolves and `judgeCandidate` accepts, `candidate.ChangeSet(ctx, \\\"HEAD\\\")` refuses a run whose candidate is left uncommitted, naming the paths.\\n\\n**5. Tests** — `gitx` (real repo: non-ASCII, tab, leading/trailing space, ASCII control, renames from/to quoted paths, quoted deletion, plus `ChangeSet` against HEAD), `report` (verbatim `git diff` output for all of those; escape decoding incl. malformed refusal), `workflow` (whitespace-only differences, quoted out-of-plan modification/deletion, out-of-plan rename source, disagreement refusal, in-plan pass, a real-worktree formatter-widening test across both bindings, and structural tests pinning binding order and the commitment check's position).\\n\\n`gofmt -l cmd internal` clean, `go vet ./...` clean, `go test ./...` passes except `internal/publish TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote` — **pre-existing**: I verified it fails identically on the unmodified tree. A global `core.hooksPath` in this environment points at a leaked Sensei Code guard that denies push.\\n\\n## Three things for you, left undone rather than decided\\n\\n1. **`confineToPlan` did not exist.** The plan says \\\"change\\\" it; there is no such function anywhere in the repo or its history. I created it in `testedit.go` as specified (no new files). Consequently there was also only *one* pre-existing binding point shape, not two — I added confinement at both places the plan names.\\n\\n2. **A plan naming no files confines nothing.** The plan doesn't address the empty-plan case. Refusing every change under a fileless `modify` plan would be a large behaviour change beyond \\\"no other behaviour changes\\\", so `confineToPlan` returns nil there, with that limitation named in the doc comment rather than hidden. If you want fileless modify plans refused, that's a one-line change and your call.\\n\\n3. **The commitment rule collides with `publish.Open`.** Publication runs `git add -- \u003cpaths\u003e` then `git commit`, which fails with \\\"nothing to commit\\\" against an already-committed candidate. So once item 4 is in, every accepted candidate reaches publication already committed and publication will error. `publish.go` is outside my plan; I left it alone. Related: I have **not** committed this candidate, because the orchestrator running it is the pre-change binary whose publication path still expects an uncommitted tree.\\n\\nAlso worth knowing: a **type change** (symlink ↔ regular file) is `T` in `--name-status` but a delete+add pair in the patch, so reconciliation refuses it. That is fail-closed and the message names it precisely, but it is a narrowing the task statement doesn't mention. I did not special-case it.\\n\\nI recorded no `sensei propose` entry — a governance write isn't in the bounded plan.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go, internal/gitx/git.go) | invariants: sensei_code.candidate.reviewer_sees_every_changed_file, sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope | uncertainty: confineToPlan was specified as pre-existing but had to be authored; empty-plan confinement and the publish.go commit collision are judgement calls left to the architect\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1699,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":158858,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1699},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"387957e3-29eb-4042-bbfa-afa88be0c2c6\",\"uuid\":\"7589a943-d600-4904-bd9a-99bf6abf9616\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-30T00:32:32.573Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeXzS8WnjaUFQpPAkoBdJ\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
