{"id":"20260830T003503.967010651Z-2256fb47","time":"2026-08-30T00:35:03.967010651Z","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.finding","summary":"[f1] blocking: The new ChangeSet/reconciliation path supports Git copies and type changes. (internal/gitx/git.go: Status/nameStatus; internal/report/report.go: Status/FromDiff) — gitx.ChangeSet emits Copied and TypeChanged, but report.Status has neither value and FromDiff parses neither copy headers nor mode changes. A candidate with repository-configured copy detection or a legitimate file-mode/type change therefore necessarily disagrees with its renderer and is refused before audit or reviewer. That is an unintended scope of refusal and conflicts with Sensei’s critical requirement that the reviewer see every changed file. → Extend report.Status and FromDiff to model Git copy and type-change records (including old paths for copies), then reconcile those statuses exactly. Add end-to-end real Git diff tests for both cases.","payload":{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"The new ChangeSet/reconciliation path supports Git copies and type changes.","reference":"internal/gitx/git.go: Status/nameStatus; internal/report/report.go: Status/FromDiff","reason":"gitx.ChangeSet emits Copied and TypeChanged, but report.Status has neither value and FromDiff parses neither copy headers nor mode changes. A candidate with repository-configured copy detection or a legitimate file-mode/type change therefore necessarily disagrees with its renderer and is refused before audit or reviewer. That is an unintended scope of refusal and conflicts with Sensei’s critical requirement that the reviewer see every changed file.","correction":"Extend report.Status and FromDiff to model Git copy and type-change records (including old paths for copies), then reconcile those statuses exactly. Add end-to-end real Git diff tests for both cases.","proof_gap":"Existing tests cover only added, modified, deleted, and renamed paths; none proves a valid copied or type-changed candidate reaches review."}}
{"id":"20260830T003503.967071702Z-e1110810","time":"2026-08-30T00:35:03.967071702Z","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.finding","summary":"[f2] major: The supplied Sensei diff audit and validation evidence apply to candidate revision 9571c126451a. (candidate revision 9571c126451a; Sensei workspace status; supplied Sensei diff audit) — The live authoritative workspace receipt resolves revision f01592b0f0828605ed254047fc064f41dacc78f2, and 9571c126451a is not available in this checkout. The audit explicitly labels its input trust as caller-supplied. Thus neither the live graph check nor the audit can establish that the reviewed bytes are the named candidate revision. → Make the candidate revision available in the review workspace and produce revision-bound audit/validation receipts from it.","payload":{"id":"f2","severity":"major","claim":"The supplied Sensei diff audit and validation evidence apply to candidate revision 9571c126451a.","reference":"candidate revision 9571c126451a; Sensei workspace status; supplied Sensei diff audit","reason":"The live authoritative workspace receipt resolves revision f01592b0f0828605ed254047fc064f41dacc78f2, and 9571c126451a is not available in this checkout. The audit explicitly labels its input trust as caller-supplied. Thus neither the live graph check nor the audit can establish that the reviewed bytes are the named candidate revision.","correction":"Make the candidate revision available in the review workspace and produce revision-bound audit/validation receipts from it.","proof_gap":"No executable revision-to-diff binding is available for 9571c126451a."}}
{"id":"20260830T003503.967190168Z-7c9ee920","time":"2026-08-30T00:35:03.967190168Z","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.completed","summary":"REVISE: REVISE. Sensei is authoritative/current and its preflight names the critical invariant “The reviewer judges the whole candidate, including files the worker created.” This candidate cannot uphold that invariant for all Git-valid ChangeSet statuses, and the supplied audit is not bound to revision 9571c126451a in this workspace.  (reviewer · via codex · session fresh · candidate 9571c126451a)","payload":{"provenance":{"task_id":"task-1788049212707426532","role":"reviewer","provider":"codex","session_id":"session-20260830T002012.706816133Z","session_mode":"fresh","base_sha":"f01592b0f0828605ed254047fc064f41dacc78f2","candidate_digest":"9571c126451aba66","graph_build_commit":"fac399f8225f","at":"2026-08-30T00:35:03.96699911Z"},"decision":"revise","summary":"REVISE. Sensei is authoritative/current and its preflight names the critical invariant “The reviewer judges the whole candidate, including files the worker created.” This candidate cannot uphold that invariant for all Git-valid ChangeSet statuses, and the supplied audit is not bound to revision 9571c126451a in this workspace.","instructions":"Make report.FromDiff represent every ChangeSet status that the authoritative Git command may emit and add real-diff tests for copy and type-change cases; reconciliation must then agree rather than refuse a valid candidate before review. Also provide/materialize revision 9571c126451a and rerun the Sensei audit against that exact revision, rather than relying on caller-supplied diff evidence.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"The new ChangeSet/reconciliation path supports Git copies and type changes.","reference":"internal/gitx/git.go: Status/nameStatus; internal/report/report.go: Status/FromDiff","reason":"gitx.ChangeSet emits Copied and TypeChanged, but report.Status has neither value and FromDiff parses neither copy headers nor mode changes. A candidate with repository-configured copy detection or a legitimate file-mode/type change therefore necessarily disagrees with its renderer and is refused before audit or reviewer. That is an unintended scope of refusal and conflicts with Sensei’s critical requirement that the reviewer see every changed file.","correction":"Extend report.Status and FromDiff to model Git copy and type-change records (including old paths for copies), then reconcile those statuses exactly. Add end-to-end real Git diff tests for both cases.","proof_gap":"Existing tests cover only added, modified, deleted, and renamed paths; none proves a valid copied or type-changed candidate reaches review."},{"id":"f2","severity":"major","claim":"The supplied Sensei diff audit and validation evidence apply to candidate revision 9571c126451a.","reference":"candidate revision 9571c126451a; Sensei workspace status; supplied Sensei diff audit","reason":"The live authoritative workspace receipt resolves revision f01592b0f0828605ed254047fc064f41dacc78f2, and 9571c126451a is not available in this checkout. The audit explicitly labels its input trust as caller-supplied. Thus neither the live graph check nor the audit can establish that the reviewed bytes are the named candidate revision.","correction":"Make the candidate revision available in the review workspace and produce revision-bound audit/validation receipts from it.","proof_gap":"No executable revision-to-diff binding is available for 9571c126451a."}]}}
